What release 2026.11.5 installed

This folder is what `eva-md install` of release 2026.11.5 (tag 2026.11.5,
commit 4f5fa2c) left in a home of its own, with both host CLIs faked.
TestUpgradeFrom2026_11_5 lays it down in a test's home and runs the current
install over it.

- MANIFEST lists every folder (d), file (f) and link (l) the home held, with
  its mode, sorted by path. Git keeps neither modes, empty folders nor links
  here, so the test makes them from this list.
- home/ holds the files. The home's path is written as @HOME@ in every file
  and link target.
- The binary, home/.local/share/eva-md/bin/eva-md, is a one-line placeholder.
- fake-bin, the fake host CLIs, is left out; cli-paths.json still names them,
  as @HOME@/fake-bin/claude and @HOME@/fake-bin/codex, where the test makes
  its own.
- .config/eva-md/config.toml is setup's, written by hand before the install
  with made-up values; the install only reads it. inbox/.baseline is the time
  the install ran, so it differs on each run.

How it was made, on Linux with Go 1.26, git, perl and network access to the
Go module proxy (2026.11.5 builds against an older okf, which the module
cache may lack). Run it in the top folder of an eva-md checkout that has the
tag or the commit; nothing here touches the real home.

    set -euo pipefail
    F=$PWD/internal/install/testdata/installed-2026.11.5
    S=$(mktemp -d)
    mkdir "$S/src"
    git archive 4f5fa2c | tar -x -C "$S/src"
    (cd "$S/src" && GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly go build -buildvcs=false \
        -ldflags "-X main.version=2026.11.5" -o "$S/eva-md" ./cmd/eva-md)
    mkdir "$S/home" "$S/hosts"
    export H=$(cd "$S/home" && pwd -P)
    hosts=$(cd "$S/hosts" && pwd -P)
    mkdir -p "$H/fake-bin" "$H/.local/bin" "$H/.config/eva-md"
    chmod 700 "$H/.config" "$H/.config/eva-md" "$H/.local" "$H/.local/bin"
    printf '%s\n' "wiki_path = \"$H/eva-wiki\"" \
        'expected_remote = "github.com/example/eva-wiki"' \
        'instance = "fixture-12345678"' 'machine_label = "fixture"' \
        > "$H/.config/eva-md/config.toml"
    chmod 600 "$H/.config/eva-md/config.toml"
    # fake <host> <list> <listed> <empty> <market> <no market> <add>: a host
    # CLI that keeps eva-md's registration in $hosts, as the fake hosts of
    # cmd/eva-md/release_test.go do.
    fake() {
        local s="$hosts/$1"
        cat > "$H/fake-bin/$1" <<EOF
    #!/bin/sh
    case "\$*" in
    "$2")
        if [ -f '$s.plugin' ]; then printf '$3\n' "\$(cat '$s.market')"; else echo '$4'; fi ;;
    "plugin marketplace list --json")
        if [ -f '$s.market' ]; then printf '$5\n' "\$(cat '$s.market')"; else echo '$6'; fi ;;
    "plugin validate --strict --json "*) echo '{"success":true}' ;;
    "features list") echo 'hooks experimental true' ;;
    "plugin marketplace add "*" --json") printf '%s' "\$4" > '$s.market'; echo '{}' ;;
    "$7") : > '$s.plugin'; echo '{}' ;;
    *) exit 2 ;;
    esac
    EOF
        chmod 700 "$H/fake-bin/$1"
    }
    fake claude "plugin list --json" \
        '[{"pluginId":"eva-md@eva-md","name":"eva-md","enabled":true,"readFromFolder":"%s/plugins/eva-md","folderVersion":"1","errors":[]}]' '[]' \
        '[{"name":"eva-md","root":"%s"}]' '[]' "plugin install eva-md@eva-md --scope user --json"
    fake codex "plugin list --json --marketplace=eva-md" \
        '{"installed":[{"pluginId":"eva-md@eva-md","name":"eva-md","enabled":true,"source":{"path":"%s/plugins/eva-md"}}]}' '{"installed":[]}' \
        '{"marketplaces":[{"name":"eva-md","path":"%s"}]}' '{"marketplaces":[]}' "plugin add eva-md@eva-md --json"
    env -i HOME="$H" PATH="$H/fake-bin:$H/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" TMPDIR="$S" \
        GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 "$S/eva-md" install
    # Record the home: the manifest, then each file with the home's path
    # replaced by the token, and the binary by its placeholder.
    rm -rf "$F/home" "$F/MANIFEST"
    mkdir "$F/home"
    (cd "$H" && find . -mindepth 1 -path ./fake-bin -prune -o -print | sed 's|^\./||' | LC_ALL=C sort |
    while IFS= read -r p; do
        if [ -L "$p" ]; then
            echo "l $p $(readlink "$p" | perl -pe 's/\Q$ENV{H}\E/\@HOME\@/g')"
        elif [ -d "$p" ]; then
            echo "d $(stat -c %a "$p") $p"
            mkdir "$F/home/$p"
        else
            echo "f $(stat -c %a "$p") $p"
            if [ "$p" = .local/share/eva-md/bin/eva-md ]; then
                printf 'placeholder for the eva-md 2026.11.5 binary\n' > "$F/home/$p"
            else
                perl -pe 's/\Q$ENV{H}\E/\@HOME\@/g' "$p" > "$F/home/$p"
            fi
        fi
    done) > "$F/MANIFEST"
    rm -rf "$S"

The heredoc's lines are indented here only as this file's code block: remove
the four spaces before each line when you paste it, or the heredoc's EOF is
not found. On macOS, stat -c %a is stat -f %Lp.

Then check that no path or name of the machine that made it is left:
TestFixture2026_11_5HoldsNoRealPath does, and so does a search of the folder
for your home's path and your user name.
